Package: upcie-iommu-map-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms
Description: experimental IOMMU-map helper for VFIO GPU P2P DMA (DKMS)
 Standalone out-of-tree kernel module serving the UPCIE_IOMMU_MAP /
 UPCIE_IOMMU_UNMAP ioctls on a dedicated /dev/upcie-iommu-map misc device.
 Given a PCI BDF, an array of device-physical addresses (e.g. a
 CUDA/udmabuf-derived phys_lut), and a userspace-chosen IOVA base, it
 installs the addresses into the IOMMU domain the device currently uses.
 For a VFIO-controlled NVMe this makes GPU memory reachable for P2P DMA:
 userspace builds NVMe PRPs from the IOVA range.
 .
 The module is an experimental proof of concept. It borrows a live IOMMU
 domain it does not own and bypasses VFIO and iommufd IOVA accounting; see
 the README for the strict mapping and lifetime requirements. Built and
 installed via DKMS, it rebuilds automatically on kernel updates with no
 custom kernel required.
